    <article>
      <h3>
        About Etch-a-Sketch
      </h3>
      <p>
        Inspired by the classic mechanical drawing toys of the 20th century, this digital version brings that nostalgic knob-turning experience to your browser. The constraint of horizontal and vertical movement creates a unique creative challenge.
      </p>
      <p>
        The left knob moves the stylus horizontally, while the right knob moves it vertically. Creating curves and diagonal lines requires careful coordination of both knobs simultaneously.
      </p>
      <h3>Using This Digital Version</h3>
      <p>
        Drag the knobs in circles to draw - clockwise moves in the positive direction. You can also use arrow keys for precise control. The knobs rotate as you use them!
      </p>
      <p>
        You can save your creations as images and share them. Click the trash icon to shake it clean and start over.
      </p>
      <h3>Tips for Better Drawings</h3>
      <p>
        Start with simple geometric shapes to get a feel for the controls. Stairs, buildings, and blocky letters work well with the horizontal/vertical constraint. For more advanced drawings, practice smooth coordination between both knobs to create diagonal lines and curves.
      </p>
    </article>
